  "notes": "USAGE:\nThe kanji {淹|い} specifically means to brew by steeping or pouring hot water. In practice, ⟦お{茶|ちゃ}→お茶：00576_ocha⟧⟦を→を：00422_wo⟧⟦{入|い}れる→入れる：01098_ireru⟧ (using the simpler kanji) is also very common and accepted. Using {淹|い}れる signals a more deliberate focus on the brewing process itself.\n\nApplies to tea (⟦{緑茶|りょくちゃ}→緑茶：10971_ryokucha⟧, ⟦{紅茶|こうちゃ}→紅茶：02878_koucha⟧, etc.) and coffee. Not used for other beverages.\n\nCOMMON COLLOCATIONS:\n- ⟦お{茶|ちゃ}→お茶：00576_ocha⟧⟦を→を：00422_wo⟧{淹|い}れる: to brew tea\n- ⟦コーヒー→コーヒー：00789_koohii⟧⟦を→を：00422_wo⟧{淹|い}れる: to brew coffee\n- ⟦{丁寧|ていねい}→丁寧：00896_teinei⟧⟦に→に：00314_ni⟧{淹|い}れる: to brew carefully\n- {淹|い}れたて: freshly brewed",
